.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt AR 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ar
.Nd create, list and extract POSIX archives
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl r|t|x|s
.Op Fl vc
.Ar archive
.Op Ar members ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility manages the portable
.Ql !<arch>\n
archive format.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl r
Replace members in the archive, appending members that are not present.
.It Fl t
List member names.
.It Fl x
Extract members into the current directory, restoring their mode.
.It Fl s
Rewrite the ELF symbol table.
.It Fl v
Verbose listing/extraction.
.It Fl c
Accepted compatibility flag; archive creation is silent.
.El
.Pp
Short member names use
.Ql name/ ;
longer names use the
.Ql #1/<len>
extension.
A
.Ql /
member carries a simple symbol table for ELF32/ELF64 little-endian objects.
Operations
.Fl d ,
.Fl m ,
.Fl p ,
.Fl q
and
.Fl u
are not implemented and are reported as usage errors.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A missing or malformed archive exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uuencode 1 ,
.Xr uudecode 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the POSIX archive format with the documented subset.
